## Summary

I delivered a production-quality native Apple (SwiftUI + Swift Charts) implementation of **`ChargingSessionDetailWidget`** at parity with the web source, committed as `9ae836c1`.

**What was built** (`apps/apple/Sources/Dashboard/Widgets/` — the actual compiled source root per `project.yml`, reconciled from the prompt's nominal path so it genuinely builds/tests):
- `ChargingSessionDetailWidget.swift` — surface entry, `Size` (registry 2×4/min/max + clamping), shell chrome, previews
- `+Views.swift` — freshness chip, compact body, stat summary, dual-axis power+SoC chart (Swift Charts analog of the web `ComposedChart`)
- `+Projection.swift` — pure, framework-free adapter (charger classification, duration derivation, W→kW, SoC interpolation, stats, formatting) + view state
- `+Model.swift` — `@Observable` binder to the KMP `ChargingStore`/`VehiclesStore` (P1/S8) via `FlowBridge`/`LoadableState`; emits the `screen_view` diagnostics event (P1/S11)
- `ChargingSessionDetailWidgetTests.swift` — adapter + per-state render + a11y/metadata tests
- 21 new `Localizable.xcstrings` keys (all 9 source strings + charger/unit/freshness/a11y)

**Key parity decisions** (SI cutover): reads SI DTOs (`Wh`/`W`/`Instant`), derives duration from `started/ended` and the SoC overlay from session `start/end SoC` (SI telemetry has no per-point SoC), converting to kWh/kW only at the display boundary. Every state renders (loading/error/empty/stale/offline + compact/standard/wide); no HTTP in the view.

**Verification** (full evidence in the gate log):
- ✅ `swiftformat --lint apps/apple` (0/265), `swiftlint --strict` (0 violations/261 files), placeholder check (0)
- ✅ iOS **and** macOS apps: `** BUILD SUCCEEDED **` (compiles against the real KMP `Shared.xcframework`)
- ✅ Full iOS test run: **220 unit + 13 UI tests, 0 failures** (both `.xctest` suites passed)

**Honest status (no red-as-green):** the literal `xcodebuild build test` EXIT=0 is environmentally blocked on this shared runner — the global `xcode-select` points at CommandLineTools with no passwordless sudo, so a *post-test* `xcrun simctl` teardown returns 65 even though every test passes; and the macOS test-host needs dev signing. Both are deferred to signed/stable CI per ADR-012 and `apps/macos-pending-verifications.md`. The gate log ends with `EXIT=65 / STATUS=BLOCKED` with this evidence, while the surface itself is complete and verified green on every host-runnable code gate.

